4139533989 true] [17592186275770 1145 "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=8$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-0.4}{8}=-0.05.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1-(-0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1+0.05} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1.05} \\\\  & =\\frac{800}{105} \\\\  & =\\frac{160}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275772 13194139533989 true] [17592186275771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275773 13194139533989 true] [17592186275771 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533989 true] [17592186275771 1041 "field-1" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275771 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275773 13194139533989 true] [17592186275771 1110 #uuid "3c5605b1-eb69-55a5-b2ed-13c40679dc6d" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275772 1034 "\\frac{160}{19}" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533989 true] [17592186275772 1111 #uuid "e0522c5a-4e17-5ded-8110-b77d569c0e45" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275773 1034 "\\frac{160}{21}" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533989 true] [17592186275773 1111 #uuid "539f08d6-5a09-5c3f-8f7c-f85d512a89eb" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275774 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275775 13194139533989 true] [17592186275774 1089 "q-353146" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275774 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533989 true] [17592186275774 1100 "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n1.5+1.2+0.96+0.768+⋯.\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275774 1113 #uuid "92c6649b-02e3-53cb-8890-9951a5abc116" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275774 1145 "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=1.5$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1.2}{1.5}=0.8.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{1-0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.2} \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275776 13194139533989 true] [17592186275775 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533989 true] [17592186275775 1041 "field-1" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275775 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275776 13194139533989 true] [17592186275775 1110 #uuid "d79b536d-ca46-5515-a75d-1a58b28eaeb5" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275776 1034 "7.5" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533989 true] [17592186275776 1111 #uuid "8f4c45c0-bf9f-5f40-a095-26d6775de861" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275777 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275778 13194139533989 true] [17592186275777 1089 "q-40310" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275777 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533989 true] [17592186275777 1100 "Consider the negative infinite geometric sequence that has a third term equal to $-1$ and a seventh term equal to $-\\frac{1}{4\\,096}.$ What is the sum to infinity of the terms of this sequence?\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that $4\\,096={8}^{4}.$*" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275777 1113 #uuid "ecb72902-5e9e-57ac-8d4a-9417265e93b4" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275777 1145 "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFrom the question statement we have ${a}_{3}=-1$ and ${a}_{7}=-\\frac{1}{4\\,096}.$ We can find the common ratio using the following formula:\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the known information into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{7-3} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{4\\,096})}{(-1)} \\\\ {r}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{4\\,096} \\\\ {r}^{4} & ={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{4} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[4]{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{4}} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have taken the positive fourth root since we're told that the sequence is negative.\n\nNow, using the formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}\n$$\n\nfor the $n$th term of the geometric sequence, we can find the first term. Indeed, for $n=3$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{2} \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{2} \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}(\\frac{1}{64}) \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{-64}{(1-\\frac{1}{8})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{64}{(\\frac{7}{8})} \\\\  & =-64\\cdot \\frac{8}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{512}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275779 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275780 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275781 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275782 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275783 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1041 "selection" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275783 13194139533989 true] [17592186275778 1110 #uuid "a3fae6b5-8536-547d-bf06-f9189c3b9375" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275779 1034 "-\\frac{32}{3}" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533989 true] [17592186275779 1111 #uuid "82e95abf-1ce8-514e-ac39-d2d3233842d2" 13194139533989 true] [17592186275780 10